{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"silky-devoted-kangaroo","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## The defect\n\n`tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py::test_ac2_round_b_iac_recommendation_routing_gets_tools_once_whole_module`\nand `::test_ac6_sidecar_deps_include_terraform_reads_and_hash_only_changes_when_they_change`\nhard-require the OPTIONAL `grounding-terraform` extra (`python-hcl2`) with **no\n`pytest.importorskip` guard**, so they redden every lean CI lane.\n\nThe file's author added a guard to THREE of its tests (lines 230, 304, 402) and missed these two —\nwhich are exactly the two that drive a real HCL parse.\n\nFailing now on main (run 33929382057, sha `6c2267d8d`), in `sweep (declared lower-bound\nresolution)` and `sweep (py3.15)` with byte-identical output:\n\n```\nFAILED ...::test_ac2_round_b_iac_recommendation_routing_gets_tools_once_whole_module\n  AssertionError: assert 'abstain' == 'refuted'\nFAILED ...::test_ac6_sidecar_deps_include_terraform_reads_and_hash_only_changes_when_they_change\n  AssertionError: assert 'infra/variables.tf' in {'infra/main.tf': '12f5d85028...'}\n2 failed, 15428 passed, 96 skipped in 499.01s\n```\n\nThe install step SUCCEEDED — this is not base drift.\n\n## Verified both directions in a lean worktree\n\n`make install` = `dev,metrics`, no `grounding-terraform`:\n- without `hcl2`: **2 failed, 7 passed, 3 skipped** — the CI failures reproduced exactly\n- after `uv pip install python-hcl2==8.1.3`: **12 passed** — so the extra is the whole cause; there\n  is no product bug\n- after adding the two guards and purging `hcl2`+`lark`: **7 passed, 5 skipped, 0 failed**\n\n## WHY NO IMPORT-BASED SWEEP CAN FIND THIS CLASS\n\n**These tests never `import hcl2`.** They call rebar code that FAILS OPEN when the extra is absent:\n`terraform_tools.open_session` sets `pending=\"missing_extra\"` and every query then returns a closed\nabstention. So the symptom is a **wrong VALUE, not an ImportError**.\n\nAny sweep keyed on imports will keep missing them. That is why this recurred one commit after the\nprevious instance was fixed.\n\nEqually, `tests/_extra_guard.py` **structurally cannot** catch it: it hardens `importorskip` calls\nthat already EXIST. A test with no guard at all is invisible to it.\n\n## The sweep that WAS done, and its authority\n\n1. **AST census** of both terraform workflow test files: both use PER-TEST guards, no module-scope\n   guard. The three other terraform test modules (`tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_index.py`,\n   `tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_tools.py`,\n   `tests/unit/plan_review/test_terraform_pass1_production_wiring.py`) each carry a MODULE-SCOPE\n   guard — the per-test style is where misses happen.\n2. **Empirical whole-tier sweep, already performed by CI**: both lean sweep lanes ran the FULL unit\n   tier on a lean install and produced exactly these two failures. That is the authoritative sweep\n   for the missing-`grounding-terraform` case, and it says there are no other latent instances\n   today.\n3. **Extras delta**: gating installs `dev+reviewbot+ui+grounding-terraform` with\n   `REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1`; lower-bound sweep installs `.[dev,agents]`; macOS/Windows sweeps\n   install `.[dev,reviewbot,ui]`. **`grounding-terraform` is the ONLY extra present on the gating\n   lane and absent from EVERY sweep lane**, so it is the only extra that can produce this\n   asymmetry. Extras absent everywhere (`grounding`, `grounding-t2`, `tracing`, `pricing`,\n   `jira-datacenter`, `s3`) cannot hide a latent failure, because a test needing them would already\n   be red on all lanes.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 - `test_ac2_…` and `test_ac6_…` each carry a FUNCTION-SCOPE `pytest.importorskip(\"hcl2\")`\n      as their first statement.\n- [ ] AC2 - On an install WITHOUT `grounding-terraform`, the file reports **7 passed, 5 skipped,\n      0 failed**. Demonstrate with real output.\n- [ ] AC3 - On an install WITH the extra, the file reports **12 passed** — no coverage is lost on\n      the gating lane. Demonstrate with real output.\n- [ ] AC4 - `test_ac7_missing_extra_abstains_fail_open_and_gate_still_returns_ordinary_verdict`\n      remains UNGUARDED and still RUNS on lean lanes. It asserts the abstain path, and a lean\n      install is the real-world condition it models — guarding it (or hoisting to module scope)\n      would skip it exactly where it matters.\n\n## Why per-test rather than module-scope\n\nDeliberate, per AC4: a module-scope guard would skip `test_ac7`, whose whole purpose is to assert\ncorrect behaviour when the extra is ABSENT. On the gating lane the added guards are no-ops\n(`hcl2` installed), so coverage is unchanged there, and the strict `importorskip` variant under\n`REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1` still hard-errors if the extra is ever dropped.\n\n## Relationship to other tickets\n\n`wellmade-surprised-chihuahua` (`87b8-1339-383f-43f6`) is CLOSED and covered only the plan-review\nfile. `trustful-combative-grackle` (`9c64-7582-ffad-4fea`) is OPEN and covers the STRUCTURAL gap\n(nothing ties sweep-lane extras to the gating lane's) and explicitly puts the guard fix out of\nscope. Neither covers this.\n\n**This recurrence strengthens the case for `trustful-combative-grackle`**: the guard fix landed and\nmain went red again within ONE commit, because the real defect is that a new file can require an\nextra no sweep lane installs and nothing notices until CI is already red.","id":"2862-d23d-4c13-4d7c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_ac2 and test_ac6 in test_terraform_code_review_tools.py hard-require the optional grounding-terraform extra with no importorskip guard, reddening every sweep lane"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788565372151064001,"uuid":"a6545d39-dcda-42f7-80a5-f6d4a66e40dc"}